OminX
=====

OminX is a Debian 13 (Trixie) amd64 live desktop with Cinnamon, an installer,
core desktop apps, a Debian/Flatpak software center, Steam/Proton support,
Wine/Lutris, compressed zram memory, and per-game Feral GameMode.

OminX Aurora is an original dark visual system built from midnight surfaces,
sea-glass highlights, sky-blue light, and restrained violet accents. The slim
top command bar places the OminX Launcher and workspace overview at the left,
running apps in the center, and system indicators and clock at the right. The
launcher provides pinned apps, recommendations, responsive search, an all-apps
view, and session power options. Its installed-app index is deferred until
needed, and larger search results are added in batches.

OminX Store presents app and game discovery, categories, Library, and Updates.
Real catalog searches, installs, and package operations are delegated to GNOME
Software's Debian and Flatpak backends. OminX Settings organizes native Linux
controls into Workspace, Devices, Connectivity, Appearance, Applications,
Accounts, Time & input, Gaming, Accessibility, Privacy & security, and Updates.

Nemo (Files) uses a details/list view with folders first, double-click
navigation, a Places sidebar, breadcrumb path, toolbar search/new-folder actions,
and a status bar. Home, Computer, Trash, mounted volumes, and Network icons are
available on the desktop. Shortcuts include Super+E for Files, Super+R for Run,
Super+I for OminX Settings, Ctrl+Shift+Esc for System Monitor, Super+D for Show
Desktop, Super+L to lock, Super+Tab for the workspace overview, Super+Left/Right
to tile, Super+Up/Down to maximize/restore, and Super+Shift+S for an area
screenshot. Super is usually the Windows-logo key on PC keyboards.

Start with the OminX Welcome application. Compatibility and performance notes
are in compatibility.md and performance.md. Full build instructions are in the
project README at:
https://github.com/ma19031435-eng/OminX-Linux

Automated ISO builds include build-info.txt in this directory. It records the
source commit, GitHub Actions run ID, branch, and UTC build time for that image.

The base system and bundled applications retain their upstream licenses and
identities. OminX does not include Microsoft code or claim that every Windows
application is compatible. No universal 50% latency reduction is promised.
